{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And He became king in Jeshurun.</b> Then He who was king in Jeshurun — namely the blessed El — was king among those who draw near and those who grasp the Torah." "<b>When the heads of the people gathered.</b> At the giving of the Torah, as it says: וַתִּקְרְבוּן אֵלַי כָּל רָאשֵׁי שִׁבְטֵיכֶם וְזִקְנֵיכֶם (Deuteronomy 5:20). And as it says: הֵן הֶרְאָנוּ ה׳ אֱלֹהֵינוּ אֶת כְּבוֹדוֹ וגו׳ (Deuteronomy 5:21)." "<b>Together the tribes of Israel.</b> He was king over all the tribes of Israel together, for then they acknowledged and accepted His kingship, as they said: וְאַתְּ תְּדַבֵּר אֵלֵינוּ אֵת כָּל אֲשֶׁר יְדַבֵּר ה׳ אֱלֹהֵינוּ אֵלֶיךָ וְשָׁמַעְנוּ וְעָשִׂינוּ (Deuteronomy 5:24)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:23:32.963220132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}